{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L2CmmL24ECoAjqNJsCWZbH","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Aurora Dashboard â€” Stage 0: Intake & Framing\n2\t\n3\t**Crucible run:** greenfield-on-existing-data Â· 2026-06-11\n4\t**Deliverable target:** Foreman-ready doc-trio in `docs/foreman-handoff-dashboard/`\n5\t**Status:** ðŸš¦ GAPS RESOLVED 2026-06-11 â€” awaiting explicit North-Star lock to open Stage 1\n6\t\n7\t---\n8\t\n9\t## 1. The North Star (proposed â€” lock or amend)\n10\t\n11\t> **A locally-served, read-only web dashboard that gives John one morning view of\n12\t> Aurora's nightly multi-agent fleet â€” results and health at a glance, with a\n13\t> visual way to explore the knowledge catalog â€” so he never has to read raw\n14\t> JSON/markdown to know what the fleet found, what it cost, and what broke.**\n15\t\n16\tTwo co-equal jobs:\n17\t\n18\t1. **The morning glance** â€” \"what did the fleet do last night, is it healthy, what\n19\t   did it cost, what's worth my attention, what broke that I should look at?\"\n20\t2. **The catalog explorer** â€” \"let me *see* the knowledge graph / catalog and move\n21\t   through it visually instead of reading library markdown.\"\n22\t\n23\t**Success looks like:** John opens one local URL each morning and, in under a\n24\tminute, knows (a) the top taste-ranked finds with their why-lines, (b) fleet health\n25\t(errors/degrade/noise), (c) spend, (d) catalog size/health â€” and can click into any\n26\tof them or into a visual map of the catalog, without opening a JSON file.\n27\t\n28\t---\n29\t\n30\t## 2. The Oranges read (real-intent foresight)\n31\t\n32\tThe surface ask is \"a GUI for the reports.\" The *real* intent, read 2â€“3 steps out:\n33\t\n34\t- **John is the fleet's operator, not its reader.** Today the morning briefing is\n35\t  pushed as a session note + markdown + PDF. A dashboard is the operator console:\n36\t  it must answer \"is my fleet healthy and earning its keep?\" faster than the prose\n37\t  briefing does â€” that means **errors and degrade are first-class, not buried.**\n38\t- **This is the first tab of a future cockpit.** The explicit \"merge into Anchor as\n39\t  a tab later\" means the real deliverable is *a clean, embeddable module*, not a\n40\t  one-off page. Architecture is a North-Star criterion here, co-equal with the view.\n41\t- **The catalog viz is for trust, not decoration.** John can't eyeball 298 artifacts\n42\t  in markdown. A visual map is how he sanity-checks taxonomy coverage, taste\n43\t  distribution, and dead links â€” i.e. it's a *health* instrument too, not just pretty.\n44\t\n45\t**Inclusion test for this build:** every panel must answer one of â€”\n46\t*what's new? Â· is it healthy? Â· what did it cost? Â· what's worth my attention? Â·\n47\tcan I see the catalog?* Anything that doesn't is bloat and gets cut or deferred.\n48\t\n49\t---\n50\t\n51\t## 3. Scope ledger (Confirmed / Inferred / Gap)\n52\t\n53\t### âœ… Confirmed (from the request + the codebase)\n54\t- **C1** Standalone, locally-served web GUI. Mirror the Anchor stack: a **Python\n55\t  (Flask) server** serving an **HTML dashboard**, runnable on the server box.\n56\t- **C2** **Read-only** against `kb/aurora.db` and `reports/`. The dashboard *observes*;\n57\t  it never mutates the catalog. (Unlike Anchor, which writes back to markdown.)\n58\t- **C3** Does **not** rebuild or trigger the pipeline; it visualizes existing outputs\n59\t  + a morning refresh. Independent of the 01:07â€“06:47 nightly sweep execution.\n60\t- **C4** Does **not** surface the publisher push â€” focus is on *results/health*.\n61\t- **C5** Never reads `.env`. No secrets in the served surface.\n62\t- **C6** Must surface: morning summary (`latest_summary.json` â€” productivity /\n63\t  suggestion-adoption, `top_finds` with taste why-lines + star/badge quality,\n64\t  `finds_new`, `noise_audit`, cost rollup), `latest_briefing_note.md`, the weekly\n65\t  digest (`reports/weekly/<date>.md`), per-sweep \"what was new\"\n66\t  (`reports/{agents,tools,skills,models}/<date>/`), errors/failures John can drill\n67\t  into (sweep logs, non-zero `noise_audit`, degrade/`critic_c` counts, backfill\n68\t  audits in `reports/backfills/*.json`), and a human visualization of the\n69\t  knowledge graph / catalog (seeds: `library/_map.html`, `_model_grid.html`; data\n70\t  in `kb/aurora.db`: artifacts, taxonomy via `embeddings.domain_path`,\n71\t  `interest_score` taste, `link_health` stars, `hh_events` usage).\n72\t- **C7** Designed standalone first, but **structured to become an Anchor tab later**:\n73\t  clean module boundary, no hard Anchor coupling yet.\n74\t- **C8** Deliverable is a vetted Crucible doc-trio (Description + Master + Impl) with\n75\t  waves, Foreman-ready, in `docs/foreman-handoff-dashboard/`. Branch context:\n76\t  `foreman/aurora-revamp` (PR #6).\n77\t\n78\t### ðŸ”Ž Inferred (my defaults â€” override any at the gate)\n79\t- **I1** **Live server, read-on-request.** Flask reads the DB (read-only / `mode=ro`)\n80\t  and `reports/` on each request and renders current state, rather than baking a\n81\t  static snapshot. A lightweight fingerprint/poll (Anchor pattern) lets the page\n82\t  auto-refresh when `latest_summary.json` changes. \"Morning refresh\" = the page is\n83\t  simply correct whenever opened after the nightly run lands.\n84\t- **I2** **Port 5001** (Anchor owns 5000), bound to `127.0.0.1` only (local-only,\n85\t  no auth surface). Launch script mirrors Anchor's `python aurora_dashboard.py`.\n86\t- **I3** **Module boundary = a self-contained package** (e.g. `dashboard/` with its\n87\t  own `app` blueprint factory + a data-access layer that knows nothing about Flask),\n88\t  so \"become an Anchor tab\" = mount the blueprint + drop the panel into Anchor's\n89\t  shell. No shared globals with the sweep code; it imports read-only query helpers.\n90\t- **I4** **Read-only DB access via a thin query module** (`dashboard/queries.py`),\n91\t  opening sqlite with `file:...?mode=ro&immutable=0` and WAL-aware, never writing.\n92\t  Reuses existing helpers where they're already read-only; does not import the\n93\t  orchestrator.\n94\t- **I5** **No new heavy frontend framework.** Vanilla HTML/CSS/JS + a single small\n95\t  charting lib already proven in-repo (the `_map.html` D3 idiom), to keep it\n96\t  Anchor-embeddable and dependency-light.\n97\t- **I6** **Tests** follow the repo's pytest convention (`tests/test_dashboard_*.py`),\n98\t  data-access + route-contract level against a fixture DB; no live-KB mutation ever.\n99\t\n100\t### âœ… Gaps â€” RESOLVED (John, 2026-06-11)\n101\t- **G1 â†’ Both: map v1, graph deferred.** v1 ships the **hierarchical taxonomy map**\n102\t  (extend `_map.html`: `embeddings.domain_path Ã— kind`, color = `interest_score`\n103\t  taste, size = count, dead-link/star overlays, click-to-filter). The\n104\t  **force-directed node graph** (artifacts Ã— shared-taxonomy + `github_network_parent`\n105\t  lineage + `prov_edges` + `hh_events` usage) is **named as a deferred wave, not\n106\t  built in v1.**\n107\t- **G2 â†’ Live read-on-request (Anchor-style).** Confirms **I1**: Flask opens the DB\n108\t  read-only, reads `reports/` per request, fingerprint-poll auto-refresh. No static\n109\t  snapshot, no new nightly build step, never stale when opened.\n110\t- **G3 â†’ Signals + in-page detail.** The errors/health panel is **first-class and\n111\t  deep**: it surfaces the signals (non-zero `noise_audit`, `critic_c` degrade, `runs`\n112\t  status, backfill audit failures, dead-link count) AND renders the underlying\n113\t  detail in-page on expand â€” sweep-log tails, the backfill audit JSON, the offending\n114\t  `noise_audit`/`screen_rejects` rows â€” so John investigates without leaving the page.\n115\t  This is its own wave, not a footnote.\n116\t\n117\t---\n118\t\n119\t## 4. Premortem (what would make this build fail John)\n120\t- **PM1** It becomes a prettier briefing and *hides* failures â€” operator can't see\n121\t  what broke. â†’ Mitigation: errors/degrade are a first-class panel, not a footnote.\n122\t- **PM2** It couples to Aurora internals and can't move into Anchor. â†’ Mitigation:\n123\t  blueprint + data-access boundary is an acceptance criterion, not a nicety.\n124\t- **PM3** It writes to the live KB (lock/corruption during a sweep). â†’ Mitigation:\n125\t  read-only handle is enforced and tested; WAL coexistence verified.\n126\t- **PM4** Scope creep into a full graph-DB explorer. â†’ Mitigation: G1 picks ONE v1\n127\t  viz; the others are explicitly deferred.\n128\t- **PM5** It silently shows stale data and looks fresh. â†’ Mitigation: every panel\n129\t  stamps its source file/row time; a visible \"as of <ts>\" header.\n130\t\n131\t---\n132\t\n133\t## 5. What I am NOT planning (out of scope for this trio, unless you add it)\n134\t- Editing/mutating the catalog, retiring artifacts, or triggering sweeps from the UI.\n135\t- The publisher push / `aurora-library` distribution view.\n136\t- Auth, multi-user, or remote/hosted serving (local-only).\n137\t- Replacing the markdown/PDF briefing delivery (the dashboard is *additive*).\n138\t- Embedding into Anchor *now* (we make it embeddable; we don't do the merge in v1).\n139\t\n140\t---\n141\t\n142\t## 6. The lock\n143\t\n144\tLocking the North Star (Â§1) starts drift-detection for the rest of the run: every\n145\tlater element gets tested against it. **Please either lock Â§1 as written or give me\n146\tthe corrected wording, and answer the three Gap questions.**\n147\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"42bf37f3-9c58-475c-955a-a46cd5d98c92","uuid":"bcaa2a24-37b4-4c02-b550-c94ad2fb17ca","timestamp":"2026-06-13T12:51:28.621Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\aurora\\docs\\foreman-handoff-dashboard\\STAGE0-FRAMING.md","content":"# Aurora Dashboard â€” Stage 0: Intake & Framing\n\n**Crucible run:** greenfield-on-existing-data Â· 2026-06-11\n**Deliverable target:** Foreman-ready doc-trio in `docs/foreman-handoff-dashboard/`\n**Status:** ðŸš¦ GAPS RESOLVED 2026-06-11 â€” awaiting explicit North-Star lock to open Stage 1\n\n---\n\n## 1. The North Star (proposed â€” lock or amend)\n\n> **A locally-served, read-only web dashboard that gives John one morning view of\n> Aurora's nightly multi-agent fleet â€” results and health at a glance, with a\n> visual way to explore the knowledge catalog â€” so he never has to read raw\n> JSON/markdown to know what the fleet found, what it cost, and what broke.**\n\nTwo co-equal jobs:\n\n1. **The morning glance** â€” \"what did the fleet do last night, is it healthy, what\n   did it cost, what's worth my attention, what broke that I should look at?\"\n2. **The catalog explorer** â€” \"let me *see* the knowledge graph / catalog and move\n   through it visually instead of reading library markdown.\"\n\n**Success looks like:** John opens one local URL each morning and, in under a\nminute, knows (a) the top taste-ranked finds with their why-lines, (b) fleet health\n(errors/degrade/noise), (c) spend, (d) catalog size/health â€” and can click into any\nof them or into a visual map of the catalog, without opening a JSON file.\n\n---\n\n## 2. The Oranges read (real-intent foresight)\n\nThe surface ask is \"a GUI for the reports.\" The *real* intent, read 2â€“3 steps out:\n\n- **John is the fleet's operator, not its reader.** Today the morning briefing is\n  pushed as a session note + markdown + PDF. A dashboard is the operator console:\n  it must answer \"is my fleet healthy and earning its keep?\" faster than the prose\n  briefing does â€” that means **errors and degrade are first-class, not buried.**\n- **This is the first tab of a future cockpit.** The explicit \"merge into Anchor as\n  a tab later\" means the real deliverable is *a clean, embeddable module*, not a\n  one-off page. Architecture is a North-Star criterion here, co-equal with the view.\n- **The catalog viz is for trust, not decoration.** John can't eyeball 298 artifacts\n  in markdown. A visual map is how he sanity-checks taxonomy coverage, taste\n  distribution, and dead links â€” i.e. it's a *health* instrument too, not just pretty.\n\n**Inclusion test for this build:** every panel must answer one of â€”\n*what's new? Â· is it healthy? Â· what did it cost? Â· what's worth my attention? Â·\ncan I see the catalog?* Anything that doesn't is bloat and gets cut or deferred.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Scope ledger (Confirmed / Inferred / Gap)\n\n### âœ… Confirmed (from the request + the codebase)\n- **C1** Standalone, locally-served web GUI. Mirror the Anchor stack: a **Python\n  (Flask) server** serving an **HTML dashboard**, runnable on the server box.\n- **C2** **Read-only** against `kb/aurora.db` and `reports/`. The dashboard *observes*;\n  it never mutates the catalog. (Unlike Anchor, which writes back to markdown.)\n- **C3** Does **not** rebuild or trigger the pipeline; it visualizes existing outputs\n  + a morning refresh. Independent of the 01:07â€“06:47 nightly sweep execution.\n- **C4** Does **not** surface the publisher push â€” focus is on *results/health*.\n- **C5** Never reads `.env`. No secrets in the served surface.\n- **C6** Must surface: morning summary (`latest_summary.json` â€” productivity /\n  suggestion-adoption, `top_finds` with taste why-lines + star/badge quality,\n  `finds_new`, `noise_audit`, cost rollup), `latest_briefing_note.md`, the weekly\n  digest (`reports/weekly/<date>.md`), per-sweep \"what was new\"\n  (`reports/{agents,tools,skills,models}/<date>/`), errors/failures John can drill\n  into (sweep logs, non-zero `noise_audit`, degrade/`critic_c` counts, backfill\n  audits in `reports/backfills/*.json`), and a human visualization of the\n  knowledge graph / catalog (seeds: `library/_map.html`, `_model_grid.html`; data\n  in `kb/aurora.db`: artifacts, taxonomy via `embeddings.domain_path`,\n  `interest_score` taste, `link_health` stars, `hh_events` usage).\n- **C7** Designed standalone first, but **structured to become an Anchor tab later**:\n  clean module boundary, no hard Anchor coupling yet.\n- **C8** Deliverable is a vetted Crucible doc-trio (Description + Master + Impl) with\n  waves, Foreman-ready, in `docs/foreman-handoff-dashboard/`. Branch context:\n  `foreman/aurora-revamp` (PR #6).\n\n### ðŸ”Ž Inferred (my defaults â€” override any at the gate)\n- **I1** **Live server, read-on-request.** Flask reads the DB (read-only / `mode=ro`)\n  and `reports/` on each request and renders current state, rather than baking a\n  static snapshot. A lightweight fingerprint/poll (Anchor pattern) lets the page\n  auto-refresh when `latest_summary.json` changes. \"Morning refresh\" = the page is\n  simply correct whenever opened after the nightly run lands.\n- **I2** **Port 5001** (Anchor owns 5000), bound to `127.0.0.1` only (local-only,\n  no auth surface). Launch script mirrors Anchor's `python aurora_dashboard.py`.\n- **I3** **Module boundary = a self-contained package** (e.g. `dashboard/` with its\n  own `app` blueprint factory + a data-access layer that knows nothing about Flask),\n  so \"become an Anchor tab\" = mount the blueprint + drop the panel into Anchor's\n  shell. No shared globals with the sweep code; it imports read-only query helpers.\n- **I4** **Read-only DB access via a thin query module** (`dashboard/queries.py`),\n  opening sqlite with `file:...?mode=ro&immutable=0` and WAL-aware, never writing.\n  Reuses existing helpers where they're already read-only; does not import the\n  orchestrator.\n- **I5** **No new heavy frontend framework.** Vanilla HTML/CSS/JS + a single small\n  charting lib already proven in-repo (the `_map.html` D3 idiom), to keep it\n  Anchor-embeddable and dependency-light.\n- **I6** **Tests** follow the repo's pytest convention (`tests/test_dashboard_*.py`),\n  data-access + route-contract level against a fixture DB; no live-KB mutation ever.\n\n### âœ… Gaps â€” RESOLVED (John, 2026-06-11)\n- **G1 â†’ Both: map v1, graph deferred.** v1 ships the **hierarchical taxonomy map**\n  (extend `_map.html`: `embeddings.domain_path Ã— kind`, color = `interest_score`\n  taste, size = count, dead-link/star overlays, click-to-filter). The\n  **force-directed node graph** (artifacts Ã— shared-taxonomy + `github_network_parent`\n  lineage + `prov_edges` + `hh_events` usage) is **named as a deferred wave, not\n  built in v1.**\n- **G2 â†’ Live read-on-request (Anchor-style).** Confirms **I1**: Flask opens the DB\n  read-only, reads `reports/` per request, fingerprint-poll auto-refresh. No static\n  snapshot, no new nightly build step, never stale when opened.\n- **G3 â†’ Signals + in-page detail.** The errors/health panel is **first-class and\n  deep**: it surfaces the signals (non-zero `noise_audit`, `critic_c` degrade, `runs`\n  status, backfill audit failures, dead-link count) AND renders the underlying\n  detail in-page on expand â€” sweep-log tails, the backfill audit JSON, the offending\n  `noise_audit`/`screen_rejects` rows â€” so John investigates without leaving the page.\n  This is its own wave, not a footnote.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Premortem (what would make this build fail John)\n- **PM1** It becomes a prettier briefing and *hides* failures â€” operator can't see\n  what broke. â†’ Mitigation: errors/degrade are a first-class panel, not a footnote.\n- **PM2** It couples to Aurora internals and can't move into Anchor. â†’ Mitigation:\n  blueprint + data-access boundary is an acceptance criterion, not a nicety.\n- **PM3** It writes to the live KB (lock/corruption during a sweep). â†’ Mitigation:\n  read-only handle is enforced and tested; WAL coexistence verified.\n- **PM4** Scope creep into a full graph-DB explorer. â†’ Mitigation: G1 picks ONE v1\n  viz; the others are explicitly deferred.\n- **PM5** It silently shows stale data and looks fresh. â†’ Mitigation: every panel\n  stamps its source file/row time; a visible \"as of <ts>\" header.\n\n---\n\n## 5. What I am NOT planning (out of scope for this trio, unless you add it)\n- Editing/mutating the catalog, retiring artifacts, or triggering sweeps from the UI.\n- The publisher push / `aurora-library` distribution view.\n- Auth, multi-user, or remote/hosted serving (local-only).\n- Replacing the markdown/PDF briefing delivery (the dashboard is *additive*).\n- Embedding into Anchor *now* (we make it embeddable; we don't do the merge in v1).\n\n---\n\n## 6. The lock\n\nLocking the North Star (Â§1) starts drift-detection for the rest of the run: every\nlater element gets tested against it. **Please either lock Â§1 as written or give me\nthe corrected wording, and answer the three Gap questions.**\n","numLines":147,"startLine":1,"totalLines":147}}}
